- hosts: localhost
  tasks:
    - name: "Sending Mail"
      community.general.mail:
        host: smtp.gmail.com
        port: 587
        sender: "your@gmail.com"
        to: "recipient@example.com"
        subject: "Test Mail from Ansible-Playbook"
        body: "Hi!!! This side Prateek. I am sending you mail by using ansible-playbook."
        username: "your@gmail.com"
        password: "your-generated-app-password"




1.    Go to your Google Account settings.
2.    Navigate to the “Security” section.
3.    Under “Signing in to Google,” enable “2-Step Verification” if not already enabled.
4.    In the same “Security” section, find the “App passwords” option.
5.    Click on “App passwords” and select the app “Mail” and the device “Other (Custom name)”.
6.    Click “Generate” to create an App Password.
7.    Copy the generated App Password. This will be used in your Ansible playbook.
